rithm", "order": 1}, "Extra": {"value": "<img src=\"cad6733a3132da5a71f6bab69e0c535d.svg\"><br><br><div><b>- CT scan:</b> detects abdominal fluid, solid organ injury, retroperitoneal hematomas</div><br><div><b>- FAST: </b>detects hemoperitoneum [<u><b>note:</b></u> FAST is done on <u>stable</u> patients in penetrating trauma] </div><br><div><b>- DPL: </b>aspirate abdomen to see if you can get fecal material / blood which implies something blew up. <i>DPL is only used for <u>blunt</u>, NOT penetrating abdominal trauma evaluation (<u>penetrating</u> trauma warrants immediate <b>surgical laparotomy</b> in this scenario)</i></div><br><div>- Contrast with <u>penetrating abdominal trauma</u>: if unstable then ex-lap</div>\n<br><div><img src=\"2bd555aa6b6407b7d511f9909c63ad54.webp\" style=\"width: 1000px;\"><br></div><div><img src=\"15a4c3264767711e8c3f75f34c39f5f5.webp\" width=\"716\"><br></div><span style=\"font-size: 8pt;\">Last updated: April 27, 2024</span>", "order": 2}, "Personal Notes": {"value": "", "order": 3}, "Missed Questions": {"value": "", "order": 4}, "I0": {"value": "[#!occlusions [[rect0::364,73,77,27]]<br>[[rect0::92,463,147,27]]<br>[[rect0::559,193,157,27]]<br>[[rect0::579,463,77,27]]<br>[[rect0::294,313,147,27]] #]<br>active", "order": 5}, "ankihub_id": {"value": "b052c2ca-106e-49c0-adcb-1f2c25b94c2d", "order": 6}}, "modelName": "IO-one by one (AnKing Step Deck / AnKingMed)", "mod": 1782836111, "cards": [1782836139495]}], "error": null}